\begin{title}
3. Conclusions
\end{title}

The results show that the crystal structure of FeNiCuMn- TiSnx transforms from mixed intermetallic compounds to a single crystal structure with the increasing of Sn content. The structure of FeNiCuMnTiSn alloy is composed of TiNi2Sn phase and Cu3Sn phase both of which are zinc blende structure. TiNi2Sn phase locates in dendrite region and Cu3Sn phase locates in indendrite region. TiNi2Sn phase is nonmagnetic, while Ni atoms are replaced by Fe atoms, the magnetism of the alloys appears. The magnetization of FeNiCuMnTiSnx alloys increases from 0.34 to 15.8 emu g 1 with the increasing of Sn content. The magnetic transforma- tion undergoes from the paramagnetism to superpara- magnetism and ultimately to soft magnetism with the increasing of Sn content.

